    origin: "Composting fallen leaves and straw to feed the trees is old work left by the silkworm households. The mulberry was the ration field of the silkworm room: leaves were taken crop after crop, so the soil had to be repaid crop after crop. The orchard people rotted the fallen leaves and hoed weeds at the corner of the field, and once it had fermented through they turned it into the tree basins. Whatever generation the sericulture work passed to, this way of feeding the land passed with it."
